AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::setCreditLimit()
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
├── when new credit limit is zero
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput before accruing interest
├── when new credit limit exceeds uint128 max
│   └── it should accrue and then revert with MathUtilsMaxUint128Overflow during checked conversion
├── given market is not paused
│   ├── it should accrue interest before comparing the new limit with debt
│   ├── when IRM accrual fails
│   │   └── it should revert without changing the credit limit
│   └── when accrued debt exceeds the proposed limit
│       └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput and roll back accrual
├── given market is paused
│   ├── it should skip interest accrual regardless of elapsed time
│   └── it should compare the proposed limit with currently recorded debt
├── given market is frozen but not paused
│   └── it should accrue and remain callable
├── when new credit limit is less than totalBorrowed assets
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
├── when new credit limit equals totalBorrowed assets
│   └── it should succeed
└── when new credit limit is valid
    ├── it should permit increases and decreases above recorded debt
    ├── it should accept exactly uint128 max
    ├── when new value equals current credit limit
    │   └── it should still emit and leave the same value
    ├── it should update totalSupply assets and creditLimit
    ├── it should leave totalSupply shares at zero
    ├── it should not change totalBorrowed shares positions or claimableFeesAssets except through accrual
    ├── it should emit SetCreditLimit with old and new values after any AccrueInterest event
    ├── it should not query the oracle or interact with tokens or Convex
    └── it should reject and roll back an IRM reentrancy attempt
